WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.490
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.370
<i>Sodachi Oikura despises me.</i>

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.000
<i>To the point that it's like
I killed her parents or something.</i>

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.620
<i>At the same time, I find it strange...</i>

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:16.460
<i>The fact is, I don't particularly
despise Sodachi Oikura at all.</i>

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.760
<i>Why she despises me so much.</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:23.010
<i>And why I can't bring myself to despise her.</i>

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.720
<i>I ended up finding out the answers.</i>

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.180
<i>It was a truth that unfolded two years
from its onset.</i>

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:32.940
<i>And at the same time, it was a truth
that unfolded five years from its onset as well.</i>

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.850
<i>Then, mathematically...</i>

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:39.030
<i>Or perhaps similar to a mystery novel,
let's strike a dramatic pose and set up the question.</i>

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.490
<i>Prove that when Sodachi Oikura
despises Koyomi Araragi,</i>

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:46.530
<i>that Koyomi Araragi cannot bring himself
to despise Sodachi Oikura.</i>

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:50.450
<i>However, Ougi Oshino can be
left out of any consideration.</i>

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:23.050
OWARIMONOGATARI

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.010
SODACHI RIDDLE, PART ONE

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:25.510
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:27.010
701 MIDDLE SCHOOL, A PUBLIC SCHOOL
FRONT GATES

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:35.270
So this is the middle school
you attended, Araragi-senpai?

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:39.060
Now that you mention it,
an extraordinary presence can be felt here.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:44.230
Let's go, Araragi-senpai.
It was the shoe locker, right?

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:46.320
Yeah. The shoe locker.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:51.830
It's such a strange coincidence.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:57.960
Right after I hear the story about Oikura-senpai
from you, Araragi-senpai...

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:02.460
The next day, Araragi-senpai and
that very Oikura-senpai are reunited.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:04.210
It's quite a strange twist of fate.

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:04.960
STRANGE TWIST OF FATE

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.090
Well, I was surprised.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:13.890
As for me, I didn't even know
she was in the same class as me.

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:16.930
701 MIDDLE SCHOOL, A PUBLIC SCHOOL
ENTRANCEWAY

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.940
Oh, so this is it?

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:27.070
Araragi-senpai was changing shoes right here
everyday back in 7th grade.

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:28.610
This is very moving.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:30.110
It's not moving at all...

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:34.120
Why would my changing shoes
be so moving?

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:37.080
My, oh my.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:41.080
So this is a letter addressed to you, Araragi-senpai?

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:41.960
TO: KOYOMI ARARAGI IN 1-3

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.260
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:48.760
FLASHBACK

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:49.510
NAOETSU HIGH SCHOOL

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:53.720
<i>The recollected memory
is still in the middle of chaos...</i>

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:56.220
<i>Therefore, the circumstances
should be discussed first.</i>

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:00.100
<i>I mean, the circumstances
that caused me to visit my alma mater.</i>

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:06.230
Araragi, you didn't get along with her, if I recall?

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:12.070
So, I thought you should mentally prepare
before you enter the classroom.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.910
There's nothing to worry about.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:19.620
Though we didn't get along,

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:22.670
that's talking about something
from two years ago, the distant past.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:24.670
I don't care about any of that at all.

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:27.920
You sure?

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:30.550
Oikura kept asking me.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:32.800
"How is Araragi doing right now?"

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.930
"What is Araragi doing right now?"

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:37.560
"What kind of person is Araragi now?"

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.850
"Has he grown taller?"
"What kind of food does he normally eat?"

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.860
"Around what time does he arrive at school?"

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.020
That's asking way too much...

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.360
I thought it'd be strange not to answer,

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:52.400
so I answered
the harmless kind of questions.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:53.150
HARMLESS KIND

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:59.160
And, it seemed a bit threatening,
so I didn't tell her about Senjyogahara, either.

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:00.410
Araragi.

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:06.040
Before Senjyogahara arrives at school,
you should at least have a goal set for all this.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.300
But just hold on a second, Araragi.

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:17.720
I have to go discuss the matter of Oikura's return
to school with Ms. Hoshina right now.

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:20.310
So I have to go to the teacher's office.

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:23.480
You want to come with me, Araragi?
After all, you're the class vice-president.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:28.480
I'll have the matter with Oikura resolved
before you come back.

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:31.740
Six months until we graduate.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:34.990
I'd like to spend my adolescence in comfort.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:36.490
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:53.260
Huh?

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.170
Huh?

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:57.180
Aren't you Oikura?

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:58.800
Yeah, you are Oikura!

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:00.350
Man, you surprised me!

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:03.350
If it isn't Oikura,
who was in my first-year class,

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:06.140
in the distant past
known as two years ago!

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:10.110
Do you remember me?
I'm sure you've already forgotten.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:12.900
You know, I was attendance number 2. I'm Araragi!

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:13.740
ATTENDANCE NUMBER / NAME
1 / KEIRI ASHINE
2 / KOYOMI ARARAGI
3 / BIWA ARIKURE
4 / MICHISADA IGAMI

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:16.740
I do remember.

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:19.120
Of course.

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.870
You are someone...

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:26.750
...that I would never forget about.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:31.460
SODACHI OIKURA

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:32.960
Araragi.

00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:39.840
I'm glad you remember me.

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:43.560
As previous attendance number 2,
I, Araragi, am happy.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:46.600
You seem to be doing well, unlike me.

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:48.980
Really, you make me jealous.

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:51.310
While I was cooped up
in my own house,

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:54.610
you studied, decided to try for college,
got a girlfriend...

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:58.490
Araragi, your life is truly
one of smooth sailing.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:00.740
Thanks to you.

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:02.580
Thanks to me?

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:05.660
Thanks to me?

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:11.000
I haven't been to school this whole time.
What are you saying I did for you?

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:12.710
Well, that's...

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:17.090
Well, I'm sure that you'd be able
to go to any college you wanted, Araragi.

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:18.380
If you felt up to doing so.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:20.760
Th-That's not really true.
I'm hard pressed to get in anywhere.

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:25.470
You don't have to be so humble.
You still excel at mathematics, aren't you?

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:29.980
You feel the name "Euler" is more fit for you
than for me, don't you?

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:35.530
Well, math is more like my only hope,
rather than something I'm good at...

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:39.400
You getting a girlfriend...
That must be thanks to mathematics as well.

00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:42.280
No, of all things, that's—

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:44.030
It is thanks to mathematics.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:47.290
Someone like you really pisses me off.

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:50.040
No matter how big of a grudge I hold,
it can't be enough.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:53.170
I can't help that feelings of hatred
well up, one after another.

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:55.300
It's a bottomless spring of hatred.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:59.170
For someone like me....
Come on, it can't be that much.

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:01.430
I hate that attitude of yours.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:04.930
You try to roll anything and everything up
in an ambiguous manner.

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:06.060
You compromise.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.560
You round things up nicely.

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:09.270
Back then as well, you—

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:14.150
Don't touch me.

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:17.780
I don't want the likes of you
to be worried about me.

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:22.280
There's absolutely nothing special about
someone like you being worried about me.

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:25.780
Is that so?

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:31.540
You... You seem to have quite a hatred
for people who are happy.

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:34.460
I do like people who are happy.

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:37.050
Looking at them
makes me feel happy.

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:40.550
What I despise are people
who don't know the reason for their happiness.

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:44.300
Those that don't even think about
why they're happy.

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:47.930
I despise water
that thinks it boiled itself on its own.

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:48.430
DESPISE

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:51.180
I despise seasons
that think they cycle naturally.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:51.690
DESPISE

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:54.440
I despise the sun
that thinks it rose on its own.

00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:55.060
DESPISE

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:58.690
Despise, despise, d-d-despise...
I despise them.

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:00.940
I despise you.

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:02.950
Oikura...

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:10.250
Because someone like you
is influencing others,

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:13.710
no one's reaching out to me,
no matter how much time passes.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:18.090
I despise people who think they're living
using only their own power...

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:21.590
People can't be happy
unless someone else saves them.

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:23.970
An idiot that can't even understand that...

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:26.340
I despise them, despise them so much
I feel like I'm going to die.

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:27.100
WHAT HAD CORNERED HER TO THIS EXTENT?

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:27.850
WAS IT THAT CLASS ASSEMBLY AFTER ALL?

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:28.600
OR WAS IT THE TWO YEARS OF GLOOM
SHE SPENT AFTERWARDS?

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:30.390
You're right.

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:33.850
Things like people saving themselves
on their own never happen.

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:36.440
I always think about that, too.

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:39.150
I can't forgive the ungrateful
that feel like they're living alone—

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:44.320
The one I can't forgive is you, Araragi.
I can't think of anyone more ungrateful than you.

00:09:44.530 --> 00:09:47.820
It's all self-righteous...
That's what your sense of justice is.

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:49.410
Sense of justice?

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:52.250
Or are you saying that you still remember?

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:55.040
About the contents of your shoe locker
back in 7th grade?

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:57.420
See, just as I thought.

00:09:57.710 --> 00:10:00.800
You don't remember anything, Araragi.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.550
You don't know what you're made up of.

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:05.550
I DON'T KNOW WHAT I'M MADE UP OF.

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:08.090
Oikura, what do you mean by that?

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:13.770
There is no meaning!

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:15.390
I despise meaning!

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:17.480
I despise anything and everything!

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:21.900
I despise, I despise, I despise, I despise, I despise,
I despise, I despise, I despise, I despise.

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:22.730
I despise!

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:23.440
I despise!

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:24.150
DESPISE

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:24.900
I despise!

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:25.650
I despise!!

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:33.040
I told you not to touch me!

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:49.800
WHETHER IT WAS BEFORE SHE FINISHED HER BUSINESS,
OR AFTER SHE WAS DONE WITH HER BUSINESS,
WAS SOMETHING THAT WAS UNCERTAIN.

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:51.850
IN ANY CASE, SHE ENCOUNTERED SENJYOGAHARA,
WHO HAD ARRIVED AT SCHOOL.

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:53.890
THERE, HANEKAWA PROBABLY TOLD SENJYOGAHARA
THAT OIKURA HAD COME TO SCHOOL.

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:55.980
AND JUST LIKE THE WIND,
SHE HAD RUSHED OVER HERE.

00:10:58.980 --> 00:10:59.350
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:00.860
I'll kill you.

00:11:01.190 --> 00:11:04.400
I'm the only one
who can stab Araragi with stationery.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:08.360
Even though I've gotten rid of that character trait,
I can't stand having it being reused.

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:15.870
S-Senjyogahara, wait...

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:20.380
Senjyogahara.

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:25.760
I see. So that's it.

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:27.260
I get it now.

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:30.180
So, you're dating Araragi.

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:31.390
How you've fallen.

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:38.140
Hanekawa. It's all right now.
You can let go of me now.

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:40.810
I'm sorry. It's not worth it.

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:42.520
Is it really all right?

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:44.570
What? What's not worth it?

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:46.940
Are you saying that
I'm not worth that much?

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:47.440
QUESTION

00:11:47.650 --> 00:11:49.070
How high and mighty you've become.

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:52.700
You were nothing more than a sickly girl
that couldn't do anything unless I took care of you.

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:54.740
Well...

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:58.960
It is true that you did often take care of me.

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:02.080
You were always kind to people
who were below you.

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:07.090
So I take it you've recovered
from your illness, Senjyogahara?

00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:09.220
Right. Thanks to you.

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:14.850
Araragi decided to try to get into college
because you're taking care of him, I assume?

00:12:15.260 --> 00:12:18.480
If so, I suggest you stop
doing something so useless.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:21.600
He's not going to appreciate anything,
no matter what you do.

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:24.360
Well, I suppose you might be right.

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:28.490
But, well, something like that
doesn't matter at all.

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:31.490
I'm not looking to get something
in return for this, after all.

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:36.830
The fact that I want Araragi to attend
the same university as I do is my desire to begin with.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:38.750
So, I wouldn't be wishing
for anything more than that.

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:42.210
SLAP

00:12:59.810 --> 00:13:03.520
Araragi, I'm going to pass out as well.
I trust you with the rest.

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:08.610
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:10.440
Wait... Huh?

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:11.610
This is strange.

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:16.620
That flashback didn't explain why I'm here
at my middle school with you at all, you know?

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:20.370
Oh, brother.
What are you talking about, Araragi-senpai?

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:25.330
When I visited you to do the laudable act
of thanking you for yesterday's situation,

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:27.880
you told me all about it.

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:29.840
And yours truly, though unworthy,

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:35.180
audaciously suggested maybe it would be good
for you to visit your alma mater.

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:38.390
Since I was the one that made the suggestion,
I couldn't let you go alone, either.

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:43.140
Though I felt it was meddling in affairs a bit too much,
here I am, tagging along on your research trip.

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:44.890
<i>Was that so?</i>

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:53.950
Ougi... The mystery will be solved
simply by opening that envelope.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:55.530
Is that so?

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:57.160
Let's see... What do we have?

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:02.160
THE "B" ENVELOPE IS THE WRONG ONE.
DO YOU WANT TO
CHANGE YOUR CHOICE TO THE "C" ENVELOPE?

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:05.540
Araragi-senpai, what's this supposed to mean?

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:09.920
I really can't make anything of it.
Is it in code or something?

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:12.920
Rather than a code,
that's more like a quiz.

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:15.680
What are you talking about?
You haven't even seen it.

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:21.640
It's a very famous quiz,
called the "Monty Hall problem."

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:24.890
<i>Monty Hall is the name
of a TV show host.</i>

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:28.690
<i>There are three doors
labeled "A," "B," and "C,"</i>

00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:31.650
<i>and a luxurious prize is hidden
behind one of them.</i>

00:14:32.110 --> 00:14:36.150
<i>The player is able to pick
any door they like of the three.</i>

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:41.030
<i>And after they choose,
the host opens one of the other two doors.</i>

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:44.200
<i>By doing so, he informs the player
that it was the "wrong" door.</i>

00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:48.880
<i>With that information, the player
has a second chance to make a decision...</i>

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:54.960
<i>Whether to stick with the door originally chosen,
or to choose again and pick the remaining door.</i>

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:57.970
<i>That's a simple summary of this quiz.</i>

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:01.850
Ougi, what would you do?

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:04.640
You chose the "A" envelope just now, but...

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:08.020
if you were now told that
the "B" envelope isn't the right one,

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:09.980
would you change you choice to "C"?

00:15:10.810 --> 00:15:11.730
Let's see...

00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:16.240
Isn't it statistically equal
whether or not I choose to change my choice?

00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:19.160
Even if the answer
was disclosed afterwards,

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:21.620
if one of the three among "A," "B," and "C"
is the right choice,

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.990
the probability is 1/3 for each of them.

00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:29.000
The case where you were told "B" was wrong
before you made the first choice aside...

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:33.750
Indeed. But for this case,
"changing what you choose" is the correct answer.

00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:37.380
To change your answer from "A" to "C."

00:15:37.630 --> 00:15:40.260
Then, let's open the "C" envelope.

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:44.850
My, oh my. Is this a map of sorts?

00:15:44.850 --> 00:15:47.770
There seems to be some symbol
drawn on it.

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:52.810
Next, of course, we're heading to the location
that this map shows.

00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:55.530
This is a trip retracing Araragi-senpai's memory.

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:58.780
So as a tour group of people
following the footsteps of young Araragi...

00:15:59.110 --> 00:16:00.410
Yeah... That's right.

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:04.530
Let's go, Ougi.
To the location marked on the map.

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:06.200
Wait... Huh?

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:17.630
NADEKO SENGOKU

00:16:17.630 --> 00:16:18.840
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:31.600
I DESPISE WATER THAT THINKS IT BOILED ITSELF ON ITS OWN.
I DESPISE PEOPLE WHO DON'T KNOW
THE REASON FOR THEIR HAPPINESS.

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:32.600
Hmph.

00:16:33.150 --> 00:16:40.240
Did the ruins of the cram school I hear about,
the ones my uncle slept in while he was in this town,

00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:43.370
feel anything like this, Araragi-senpai?

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:45.370
Yeah... That's right.

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:46.120
AN UNGRATEFUL ONE LIVING SO CAREFREE.

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:49.120
It's rather rundown and dangerous.

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:52.370
It's not been maintained at all,
worn down by the wind and stuff.

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:56.880
In this ruined house, I had an appointment
to meet with a certain girl...

00:16:58.000 --> 00:16:59.510
I just can't comprehend this.

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:02.630
But, the fact that there are
signs a nameplate used to be here

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:06.720
means that this ruined house
used to be an ordinary residence?

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:09.560
Who knows... I don't really
know much about this area.

00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:12.940
Back around 7th grade,
I didn't really take note of such things.

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:15.190
HOUSE FOR SALE

00:17:15.190 --> 00:17:19.440
In the first place, this sign wasn't here
back when I was coming here regularly.

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:23.320
It's probably the case that the caretaker
is different than from about five years ago...

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:36.130
Now, let's hurry in, Araragi-senpai.

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:40.800
Hearing that sound just now,
the neighbors may report to the police.

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:45.260
If a police officer were to show up,
I'll give them the excuse that we got lost.

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:48.050
So Araragi-senpai,
please go along with that.

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:51.100
That's fine.
I'll make sure to play along with you.

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:54.810
Though, it's a pretty embarrassing excuse
for high school students to have lost their way.

00:17:55.190 --> 00:17:57.310
But I don't want to find myself
out in the cold.

00:17:57.310 --> 00:18:01.440
Out in the cold?
What do you mean by that?

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:05.700
Well, you see, in my case,
both my parents are police officers, so—

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:07.240
So, both your parents are police officers!

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:10.240
<i>Huh? Why did I just say that?</i>

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:13.660
Then that means there's
nothing for us to worry about.

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:17.920
If someone files a report,
and an officer rushes over here on his bike,

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:21.130
Araragi-senpai, your parents will bail us out.

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:25.880
My parents aren't the type that would
help out their little boy in times like that.

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:30.100
More like they'd never forgive injustice,
even if their own children were the source.

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:31.390
They're strict parents.

00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:33.390
When I misbehaved as a kid,

00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:36.520
they disciplined me
by dragging me to the local police box.

00:18:36.690 --> 00:18:39.480
To the police box?
That's pretty scary...

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:41.730
You could be traumatized by that.

00:18:51.740 --> 00:18:54.750
The theory that Oikura-senpai
resents the kindness

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:57.460
that you showed
during the class assembly two years ago.

00:18:57.750 --> 00:18:59.580
That can probably be disregarded now.

00:19:00.670 --> 00:19:02.840
Why, you ask? It's simple.

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:04.960
It's because Oikura-senpai
has come to school.

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:07.220
What do you mean by that?

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:10.640
Hanekawa-senpai already mentioned it.

00:19:10.890 --> 00:19:13.640
That Ms. Tetsujo had taken maternity leave,

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:17.730
and Oikura-senpai showed up at school
as if she was swapping places.

00:19:19.230 --> 00:19:23.780
In other words, because Ms. Tetsujo
is no longer at Naoetsu High,

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:26.530
I believe Oikura-senpai
is now able to come to school.

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:34.490
Basically, that means she had known
who the culprit was back then.

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:37.330
<i>Which means,
concerning the class assembly,</i>

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:40.830
<i>there are connections to why
her personality turned out the way it did,</i>

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:43.590
<i>but there's no direct link
to the reason why she despises me.</i>

00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:45.590
<i>That's what this means.</i>

00:19:47.670 --> 00:19:49.840
<i>In the first place,
if you say that she's despised me</i>

00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:53.100
<i>from the day that we first met
in the classroom for class 1-3</i>

00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:56.220
<i>she's always despised me.</i>

00:19:56.930 --> 00:20:00.600
"I despise water that thinks
it boiled itself on its own," huh?

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:03.860
In other words,
you don't know your own roots.

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:10.360
Because you've forgotten your own roots,
Oikura-senpai has serious issues with how you live.

00:20:10.570 --> 00:20:13.740
But, as you investigate further,
that's a strange story as well.

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:17.120
It's very common to find people
who have forgotten about the past.

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:18.410
Even for me.

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:22.380
Most of who I was back in grade school or middle school
is far beyond the boundaries of oblivion.

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:26.630
It even feels like
I was actually born very recently.

00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:31.380
That you were actually born very recently?
Is that the "Five-minute hypothesis"?

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:37.640
But still, why does Oikura-senpai despise
only Araragi-senpai as if you killed her parents?

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:39.140
This is strange.

00:20:39.430 --> 00:20:40.520
This is mysterious.

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:42.020
This is suspicious.

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:44.020
This is scary.

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:45.520
Scary...

00:20:45.520 --> 00:20:48.280
Yes, scary. Because...

00:20:48.570 --> 00:20:50.030
It's different.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:55.450
<i>True. When you think about
what's scary in this world...</i>

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:58.160
<i>Those that despise you
for some incomprehensible reason</i>

00:20:58.160 --> 00:21:00.410
<i>and attack you are the scariest.</i>

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:04.420
<i>There's no way to deal with it,
because you don't know the opponent's objective.</i>

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:08.760
<i>In order to fight, they say you need to know
what the opponent feels is justice.</i>

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:14.180
<i>What does Sodachi Oikura feel is righteous,
and what does she believe is justice...</i>

00:21:14.430 --> 00:21:17.350
<i>This is a journey
to figure that out as well.</i>

00:21:24.350 --> 00:21:28.070
Wow, this room is especially terrible.

00:21:28.230 --> 00:21:31.820
This place hasn't changed one bit
from five years ago. It's unchanging.

00:21:32.110 --> 00:21:34.410
It feels like... Time has stopped.

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:38.580
You see that small tea table over there, right?
That's what was being used.

00:21:38.910 --> 00:21:42.460
Used? For what? As a chair?

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:43.580
No...

00:21:43.750 --> 00:21:46.080
In the first place,
I'm not understanding this very well.

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:50.710
Why did you keep coming to this ruined house
for an entire summer, Araragi-senpai?

00:21:51.130 --> 00:21:52.880
Your actions are too mysterious...

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:55.470
Are you an adventurous
grade-school boy or something?

00:21:55.760 --> 00:21:59.220
Actions you take during childhood
are all mysterious.

00:21:59.220 --> 00:22:01.310
None of them can be really explained.

00:22:01.730 --> 00:22:03.980
I have no idea why I was doing such a thing.

00:22:04.310 --> 00:22:07.230
My train of thought was completely different
from what it is now.

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:13.990
<i>Geez... When I'm up against Ougi,
why does my tongue get so loose?</i>

00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:18.870
<i>Even if it's something that I can fudge
by making some adequate lie, if she asks, I answer.</i>

00:22:19.660 --> 00:22:21.830
<i>By the time I realize it, I'm done answering.</i>

00:22:22.250 --> 00:22:24.750
<i>In any case, I started telling the story.</i>

00:22:25.120 --> 00:22:27.580
<i>What happened here five years ago.</i>

00:22:28.040 --> 00:22:30.500
<i>Who I met... And what I was doing.</i>

00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:34.010
<i>What Koyomi Araragi is made up of.</i>

00:22:34.800 --> 00:24:20.141
<i>A story explaining that.</i>
